# --- Secret hygiene (added 2026-07-28 after account-wide secret audit) ---
# gitignore alone does not untrack already-committed files; these were
# untracked with `git rm --cached` in the same commit.
.env.local.py
.oauth_cache
data/enhanced_credentials.db
*.pem
*.backup.[0-9]*
# `*.backup.[0-9]*` requires a digit after .backup, so it never matched
# `api.pingdemo.com.key.backup` or `.key.backup` — both real TLS private keys
# that reached public history on 2026-02-22 as a result. Match any .backup, and
# key material by extension. Note gitignore does not untrack what is already
# committed: resources/keys/private_key.pem sat in HEAD for months despite the
# `*.pem` above, and needed an explicit `git rm`.
*.backup
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
